title: "pallet-bounties: charge the asset sweep in `reclaim_bounty_funds` and `close_bounty`"
doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      `reclaim_bounty_funds` and `close_bounty` empty a bounty account through
      `Config::TransferAllAssets`, but neither declared any weight for it.

      `TransferAllFungibles` walks its asset list twice and can read a balance and run a
      transfer on each visit, so its real cost grows with the number of assets the runtime
      configures. The declared weight stayed at the figure benchmarked against a runtime that
      sweeps a single native balance, which left the declared database accesses and proof size
      several times under the real ones on a runtime with more than one relevant asset.
      `reclaim_bounty_funds` is permissionless and free when it moves anything, so the gap was
      reachable by anyone.

      `TransferAllAssets` gains a `max_weight` method stating the worst-case cost of one sweep,
      priced with the host runtime's database weight. Both calls add it to the weight they
      declare, and `close_bounty` also includes it in the actual weight it reports for the
      active path.

      Runtimes that implement `TransferAllAssets` themselves must now implement `max_weight`
      too. The three implementations shipped with the pallet already do.

crates:
  - name: pallet-bounties
    bump: major
